<title>GERMANY: Hoechst says new drugs to benefit sales.</title>
<headline>Hoechst says new drugs to benefit sales.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Hoechst AG said on Wednesday that it expected new products to contribute considerably to sales at its drugs unit Hoechst Marion Roussel.</p>
<p>Hoechst said that new products contributed only two percent to total sales last year but should contribute some 12 percent in 1998. Last year HMR posted sales of 13 billion marks ($7.6 billion).</p>
<p>Hoechst also expects to post a reduction in the time it takes to move a new product from the research to the launch date.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.708 German Marks)</p>
